  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#30090\", \"PowerToys#27615\", \"PowerToys#17288\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. With only 'Use a non-primary mouse button to toggle zone activation' enabled, FancyZones activates immediately when you drag a window, and the non-primary button then toggles it off. The maintainers' answer in the older ticket (#17288) was that this is expected behavior. To get zones that stay hidden until you press a button, also enable 'Hold Shift key to activate zones while dragging'. With both options on, zones appear only after you press Shift or the non-primary mouse button. The reporters in #30090 found that changing these settings resolved it, though others there still saw the zones activate when they shouldn't. In #30090 the toggle also seemed to be remembered between drags, so the next drag started with zones active. If you need more than this, #30090 is still open for the unresolved cases.\"}",
